<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">454 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">454 CE in world history: 2 events, 1 birth, 3 deaths and 1 state founded. 161 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/420">420 CE</a><a href="/years/429">429 CE</a><a href="/years/439">439 CE</a><a href="/years/451">451 CE</a><a href="/years/454" aria-current="page">454 CE</a><a href="/years/476">476 CE</a><a href="/years/533">533 CE</a><a href="/years/534">534 CE</a><a href="/years/552">552 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-21">21 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Valentinian III murders his general Aetius</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-iii">Valentinian III</a> killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius">Flavius Aetius</a> with his own hands during a meeting in Ravenna. The West lost the commander who had checked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a>; Valentinian was himself assassinated six months later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nedao">Battle of Nedao</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Nedao was fought in 454 in Pannonia between the sons of Attila and a coalition of their former subject peoples led by the Gepid king Ardaric.</p></div></li></ol></section>
